The fix is complete and the project builds. Here's a summary of the diagnosis and patch.

## Diagnosis

The "show password" affordance is the Material `TextInputLayout`'s password toggle (`app:passwordToggleEnabled="true"`), which is only attached to the *password* field:

- `component_intro_authentication.xml` → `introPasswordLayout`/`introPasswordEdit` (+ plain `introPasswordConfirm` EditText)
- `component_authentication.xml`, `component_password.xml`, `dialog_password_entry.xml` → same pattern

Material's toggle simply swaps the `TransformationMethod` of *its own* `EditText`. The confirmation field is a separate, plain `EditText` outside the layout, so nothing ever changed its transformation method — hence it stayed masked while the password field was revealed.

The toggle exposes no state-change callback (`TextInputLayout` in material 1.1.0 only has `addOnEndIconChangedListener`, for icon *mode*), and `TextView.setTransformationMethod()` is `final`, so it can't be overridden. However, `setTransformationMethod()` internally re-sets the text, which dispatches to `TextWatcher`s — the same mechanism Material's own `PasswordToggleEndIconDelegate` uses to keep its eye icon in sync. That gives a reliable hook.

## Patch

**`Utilities/UIHelper.java`** — new reusable helper that mirrors the password field's text visibility onto any number of linked fields:

```java
public static void linkTextVisibility(final EditText passwordInput, final EditText... linkedInputs) {
    syncTextVisibility(passwordInput, linkedInputs);
    passwordInput.addTextChangedListener(new TextWatcher() {
        @Override public void beforeTextChanged(CharSequence s, int start, int count, int after) {
            syncTextVisibility(passwordInput, linkedInputs);
        }
        ...
    });
}

private static void syncTextVisibility(EditText source, EditText... inputs) {
    boolean hidden = isTextHidden(source);
    for (EditText input : inputs) {
        if (input == null || isTextHidden(input) == hidden) continue;   // no needless churn
        int selectionStart = input.getSelectionStart();                 // preserve cursor
        int selectionEnd = input.getSelectionEnd();
        input.setTransformationMethod(hidden ? PasswordTransformationMethod.getInstance() : null);
        if (selectionStart >= 0 && selectionEnd >= 0) input.setSelection(selectionStart, selectionEnd);
    }
}

private static boolean isTextHidden(EditText input) {
    return input.getTransformationMethod() instanceof PasswordTransformationMethod;
}
```

**Call sites wired up** (one line each, right after the views are resolved):
- `Activities/IntroScreenActivity.java` (`AuthenticationFragment`) — the case from the bug report (first-time setup, Password *and* PIN)
- `Preferences/CredentialsPreference.java` — settings → authentication method
- `Preferences/PasswordEncryptedPreference.java` — settings → password/PIN
- `Dialogs/PasswordEntryDialog.java` (UPDATE mode) — backup password update, same defect

## Notes

- No layout or public-API changes: IDs, view classes and styling are untouched, so existing behavior/tests are preserved.
- Sync is applied once at setup (initial state) and on every transformation change, and it's idempotent: it skips fields whose visibility already matches, so typing doesn't cause repeated work or cursor jumps.
- Switching between Password/PIN (which calls `setInputType`) also re-masks both fields consistently, matching Material's icon state.
- `./gradlew clean assembleDebug` → **BUILD SUCCESSFUL** (both `fdroid` and `play` flavors).

